{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Hey, come on back. I'll grab a few vitals before Dr. Ellison sees you.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Okay.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): What brings you in?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Itch.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Blood pressure is one eighteen over seventy six, pulse, uh, seventy eight, temp thirty six point eight celsius. Oxygen sat is ninety nine percent.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Mm.",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (DOCTOR): Hi, I'm Dr. Ellison. I'm glad you came in. The itch is what got you here, I hear. Tell me about it, um, however it comes out.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): Rash.",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (DOCTOR): Where are you seeing that rash?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Fingers.",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (DOCTOR): Between the fingers, or on the backs?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): Between.",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (DOCTOR): Anywhere else?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): Waist.",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (DOCTOR): A time of day it gets worse?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): Night.",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (DOCTOR): Has this been, uh, days or weeks?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): Weeks.",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (DOCTOR): Anyone else at home itching?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Partner.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (DOCTOR): Only your partner?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): Kid too.",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (DOCTOR): So for weeks there's been an itchy rash between the fingers and at the waist, worse at night, and your partner and your kid at home are itching too.",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any fever with this?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (DOCTOR): How about your breathing, any cough or chest tightness?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (DOCTOR): Has your weight changed?",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): Maybe.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (DOCTOR): Did you try any cream or pill for the itch?",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): Cream.",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (DOCTOR): What was it called?",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): Hydrocortazone.",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (DOCTOR): Hydrocortisone, the one percent from the store, for the itch. Still using it?",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): Stopped.",
  "[SEG0037] person_3 (DOCTOR): When did you stop?",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (PATIENT): Last week.",
  "[SEG0039] person_3 (DOCTOR): Did anyone ever hand you ivermectin pills?",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0041] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any allergies to medicines or creams?",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0043] person_3 (DOCTOR): Itchy spots between the fingers and at the belt line, and your partner and child itching, that makes me think of scabies. It could be eczema, or a soap you all came in contact with. Umm, I'm not calling it until I look.",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (PATIENT): Okay.",
  "[SEG0045] person_3 (DOCTOR): I see little bumps and a couple of thin burrows between the fingers, and scratch marks along the waist. I don't see any pus. Those burrows, with the whole household itching, this is most likely scabies.",
  "[SEG0046] person_2 (PATIENT): Huh.",
  "[SEG0047] person_3 (DOCTOR): We'll treat it with permethrin cream, 5 percent. You coat all the skin from the neck down, between the fingers, under the nails, the waist, the belly button, and the soles. Leave it on eight to fourteen hours, then wash it off in the morning. Do that same thing one more time in a week.",
  "[SEG0048] person_2 (PATIENT): Okay.",
  "[SEG0049] person_3 (DOCTOR): Your partner and your child need the same cream the same night, or you'll pass it back and forth. Wash the sheets, towels, and clothes from the last few days on hot, and dry them hot. Stuff you can't wash goes in a sealed bag for three days.",
  "[SEG0050] person_2 (PATIENT): Bag.",
  "[SEG0051] person_3 (DOCTOR): Yeah, a plastic bag, three days. If you're still itching in two weeks, come back and see me. Don't pile on extra cream, the itch can stick around after the mites are dead.",
  "[SEG0052] person_2 (PATIENT): Okay.",
  "[SEG0053] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Want me to send the permethrin over to the Oak Street pharmacy?",
  "[SEG0054] person_3 (DOCTOR): Yes, please.",
  "[SEG0055] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0056] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): I'll send it now. Should be ready this afternoon."
 ],
